Apple today released new beta firmware for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods/">AirPods 4</a>, AirPods Pro 2, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods-pro/">AirPods Pro 3</a>. The firmware is limited to developers at the current time, and it has a build number of 9A5292e.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-803706" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2021/06/AirPods-Pro-Beta-Firmware-2.jpg" alt="" width="2250" height="1266" /><br/>
In <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, iPadOS 27, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a>, Apple is adding a new AirPods interface and support for custom EQ. AirPods are also compatible with the new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI.<br/>
<br/>
With <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-26/">iOS 26</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipados-26/">iPadOS 26</a>, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-26/">macOS Tahoe</a>, Apple added a beta firmware update installation option that's available from the AirPods settings interface when the AirPods are connected to an iPhone, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a>, or Mac, which facilitates beta testing.<br/>
<br/>
